{
  "id": "ss.fx.shell-burst",
  "name": "Shell burst",
  "description": "Where a Bombardier's shell comes down. The shell is a hot bead of the beetle's own chemistry — ember, the colour of the mortar on its back — so this is fire and not acid: a white-gold heart through ember to rust, an eight-point flare, a shock ring in `$ember`, a puff of rust-dark smoke, cinders that stay burning on the ground, and five pieces of the casing thrown out. It used to borrow the barb burst (`ss.fx.blast`), which is the acid inside a Lance's barb — two different animals' blows arriving as one green bang. Authored on the barb's contract so the game can swap one for the other: the shock ring reaches r=30 at full expansion (26 × 1.15), the number the game scales by, on an 80 canvas so the stroke never meets the edge. Nothing here is frost or magenta, for the barb's reason.",
